            <ArticleTitle>MDCT findings of intestinal ischemia due to midgut torsion without small bowel obstruction in a 12-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>236-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intestinal ischemia in the pediatric age group is a rare occurrence. We describe a case of MDCT findings of ischemia due to midgut torsion without intestinal obstruction in a 12-year-old boy, successfully submitted to surgery without any intestinal resection required.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
